.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
node_modules/
.env

# Generated artefacts. These must stay in step with gate.yaml's denylist —
# `pf check` fails if git is tracking anything the gate calls generated. They
# drifted once: the patterns here were written without `**/`, which anchors them
# to the repo root, so `groups/*/projects/*/kg/graph.duckdb` was never ignored
# and 1,622 regenerable files ended up committed.
**/target/
# `target-base/` is where the `base` dbt target's artefacts land — the second
# state Recce diffs against. The pattern is separate because `**/target/` does
# not match it.
**/target-*/
# …except the two artefacts the diff is actually measured against. They were
# called "just as regenerable as target/", and on a developer's machine they
# are. In CI they are not: capturing a baseline is a *build*, and a runner has
# code and no warehouse, so a checkout without these is a checkout whose review
# cannot run at all — which is the state six of seven projects were in. That
# makes them inputs, not output, and worth ~700 KB each.
#
# Only these two. Everything else `dbt build --target base` writes stays
# ignored, and the exception is narrow so a future artefact does not join by
# accident.
!**/target-base/
**/target-base/*
!**/target-base/manifest.json
!**/target-base/catalog.json
**/logs/
**/dbt_packages/
**/.duckdb-skills/
**/kg/*.duckdb
**/kg/*.duckdb.wal
**/kg/context_card.md
**/data/*.duckdb
**/data/*.duckdb.wal
**/reporting/queries/metrics/
# Rendered from toolkit templates by `pf evals-gen`, the same way the graph is
# rendered by `pf kg build`. Hand-written project cases sit one level up, in
# evals/cases/, and are committed.
**/evals/cases/generated/
data/pr/
.dagster/history/
.dagster/storage/
.dagster/logs/
.dagster/schedules/

# Secrets
**/.dlt/secrets.toml
**/secrets.toml
.dagster/.nux/


#dbt
dbt.log
*.log

#connection
connection.json

# The control-plane front end. `dist/` is `npm run build` output and node_modules
# is 200MB of dependencies; both are reproducible from package-lock.json.
**/ui/static/dist/
**/ui/web/node_modules/
